# Component structure

Every React component gets its own file, and every component with styles gets
its own SCSS file next to it — never append component styles to `common.scss`.

```
app/components/playground/
  Dropdown.tsx    // the component
  Dropdown.scss   // its styles, same base name
```

- Import the style file at the top of the component: `import "./Dropdown.scss";`
- Class names are global BEM-ish, prefixed by the component root class
  (`.dropdown`, `.dropdown-trigger`, `.dropdown-option`).
- Shared design tokens live in `app/_palette.scss`. Pull them in with a
  relative `@use`: `@use "../../palette" as *;`
- `app/common.scss` keeps only shared, site-wide styles (typography, page
  layout, styles reused by several components). It re-exports the palette via
  `@forward "palette";` for `global.scss`.
